## 4. 20-FOOT DISH OPTICS & ZIRCONIA INGESTION ENGINE## 4.1 The 20-Foot Modular Petal Concentrator

* Thermal Input Scale: The optical array utilizes a 20-foot wide parabolic concentrating dish, generating approximately 18 to 22 kW of pure solar thermal input at the focal point.
* Field-Serviceable Petals: The dish is split into independent geometric petals lined with a vacuum-formed, highly reflective aluminized Mylar or silver film substrate. If a section is damaged by wind-blown debris, field personnel can unpin that specific petal from the radial chassis and slide a new factory-calibrated replacement into the track in minutes.

## 4.2 Fused Quartz Optics & Zirconia (ZrO₂) Collar

* The ZrO₂ Structural Collar: The entry optics are housed within a thick, precision-machined Yttria-Stabilized Zirconia (ZrO₂) collar. With a melting point of 4,892°F (2,700°C) and low thermal conductivity, the zirconia collar acts as a structural thermal barrier, preventing intense heat from creeping into the chassis frame.
* Fused Quartz Lens & Homogenizer: High-purity fused quartz is specified for the entry lens due to its near-zero coefficient of thermal expansion, allowing it to withstand sudden shifts in solar intensity without cracking. A multi-element quartz homogenizer matrix scrambles the incoming convergent beam, converting the pin-point focus into a uniform cylinder of light that illuminates the internal ceramic walls evenly.

