## 7.1 Tapered Alumina Plug & Counterweighted J-Arm
The base of the retort features a precision-tapered hole sealed by a matching high-purity alumina ceramic plug. The plug is supported from beneath by a heavy steel J-shaped structural arm that curves around the hot drop zone, pivoting on greaseless ceramic-bushing hinges anchored to the chassis subfloor.
The rear of the J-arm features a calculated steel counterweight block that exerts continuous upward mechanical pressure, forcing the plug into its seat. The weight of the accumulating ash inside the retort strengthens this wedge seal, ensuring an airtight lock during pyrolysis.
## 7.2 Manual Drop Operation & Sealed Exterior Tray
When an operator needs to clear the ash, they pull a manual lever located outside the hot zone, pulling the counterweighted J-arm down. The alumina plug drops, and the bone-dry carbon black and sterile ash flow via gravity into a heavy-duty, 310-alloy high-temperature stainless steel collection tray.
This tray is a slide-out drawer recessed into the floor space. The operator accesses it via an exterior maintenance hatch fitted with a dual-stage compression latch and high-temperature graphite gaskets, allowing them to safely empty the sterile ash from outside without exposing the internal pod spaces to dust or fumes.
